        "description": "Born in Sicily in 1889, Frank Lentini entered the world with an extremely rare condition, he had three legs and four feet as a result of a partially developed parasitic twin. Rejected by his parents at birth, Lentini\u2019s early life was filled with hardship.\n\nBut his story didn\u2019t end there. He eventually embraced his uniqueness and became a famous performer in traveling circuses and sideshows across the United States, where audiences knew him as \u201cThe Three-Legged Man.\u201d Over time, Frank Lentini turned what many saw as a disadvantage into a remarkable life and career.\n\n#FrankLentini #History #HumanStories #RareConditions #Shorts",
